For every $L\ge2$ and every $b\in\mathbb F_3^{V_L}$, all edge and configuration blocks of $A_b$ are nonempty, and $$\label{str:size-formula}
 |A_b|=N_L=
 \sum_{e\in E_L}3^{2|F(e)|+1}
 +\sum_{v\in V_L}3^{2|F(v)|+d(v)-1}.$$ Thus $N_L$ is independent of $b$, and $$|Y_e|\le3^9,\qquad |X_v|\le3^{29},\qquad
 L^3\le N_L\le(3^{10}+3^{29})L^3.$$

The multiplication in Equation <a href="#str:group-law" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="str:group-law">[str:group-law]</a> makes $H$ a finite group. Its identity is $(0,0)$ and $(a,k)^{-1}=(-a,-k)$. The subgroup $\{0\}\times K$, identified with $K$, is central, and projection onto $C_F$ is a surjective homomorphism with kernel $K$. With the convention $[h,h']=hh'h^{-1}(h')^{-1}$, one has $$\label{str:commutator}
 [(a,k),(a',k')]
 =\left(0,\sum_{f\in F}\omega(a_f,a'_f)c^f\right).$$

Every face description $\widehat f$ on $A_b$ describes an elementary face $f$, and every elementary face has such a description. For atoms $s,s'$ on any two sides of $f$, including the same side, $$\label{grid:match-equivalence}
 \operatorname{match}_{\widehat f}(s,s')
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad u_{s,f}=u_{s',f}.$$ Consequently, for $s=(e,u,z)$ and $s'=(e,u',z')$, $$\label{grid:base-equivalence}
 \operatorname{baseEq}_{Y_e}(s,s')\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad u=u'.$$

Let $T\subseteq E$ and $\sigma\in\mathbb F_3^T$. There is a vector $k\in\ker\partial$ with $k|_T=\sigma$ if and only if every component $U$ of $G\setminus T$ satisfies $$\label{base:balance}
 R_U:=\sum_{v\in U}\sum_{\substack{e\in T\\e\ni v}}
          \epsilon_{ve}\sigma_e=0.$$ If no extension exists, some nonempty component violating <a href="#base:balance" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="base:balance">[base:balance]</a> has $$|U|\le L^3/2,
 \qquad |U|\le(|T|/c)^{3/2}.$$
